classTweaker v1 official
# Compose-in-MC feasibility spike (docs/ui/compose-in-mc-feasibility.md).
#
# ComposeSurface renders Skia into a Blaze3D TextureTarget's GL framebuffer, then blits the same
# texture (as a GpuTextureView) via BlitUvPipeline. Getting the raw GL FBO id requires the GL-backend
# classes, which Mojang ships package-private in com.mojang.blaze3d.opengl. Reflection-by-name fails
# in dev (runtime uses intermediary method names), so we widen them here and let Loom handle the
# remap. Client-only classes; only loaded when the client is running.
accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/GlDevice
accessible method com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/GlDevice directStateAccess ()Lcom/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/DirectStateAccess;
# RenderSystem.getDevice() returns the GpuDevice facade; the real GlDevice is its private backend.
accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/systems/GpuDeviceBackend
accessible field com/mojang/blaze3d/systems/GpuDevice backend Lcom/mojang/blaze3d/systems/GpuDeviceBackend;
accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/GlTexture
# MC 26.2 removed GlTexture.getFbo(DirectStateAccess, GpuTexture). FBO acquisition moved to
# GlDevice.frameBufferCache().getFbo(dsa, colorAttachments, depthAttachment). GlTexture implements
# FrameBufferAttachment, so it is passed directly as the color attachment (see ComposeSurface).
accessible method com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/GlDevice frameBufferCache ()Lcom/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/FrameBufferCache;
accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/FrameBufferCache
accessible method com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/FrameBufferCache getFbo (Lcom/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/DirectStateAccess;Ljava/util/List;Lcom/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/FrameBufferAttachment;)I
accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/FrameBufferAttachment
accessible class com/mojang/blaze3d/opengl/DirectStateAccess
